    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize the 7 of Diamonds. It is the most valuable card in the deck and contributes to the 'Most Diamonds' and 'Preme' points. Never play it unless you are certain it will be captured.\n\nPreventing Shokoba: If there is only one card left on the table (e.g., a 4), and you can't capture it, DON'T play a card that sums to a high value. Play a card that leaves the table with values that are hard to sum for the next player (like two small cards instead of one high one).\n\nThe 'Diamond Sweep': If you are trailing in points, focus entirely on the 'Most Diamonds' category. Even if you lose individual tricks, capturing 6 or 7 Diamonds will guarantee you 2 points at the end of the round (Diamond count + 7 of Diamonds).",
    Player: "Prioritize the 7 of Diamonds. It is the most valuable card in the deck and contributes to the 'Most Diamonds' and 'Preme' points. Never play it unless you are certain it will be captured.\n\nPreventing Shokoba: If there is only one card left on the table (e.g., a 4), and you can't capture it, DON'T play a card that sums to a high value. Play a card that leaves the table with values that are hard to sum for the next player (like two small cards instead of one high one).\n\nThe 'Diamond Sweep': If you are trailing in points, focus entirely on the 'Most Diamonds' category. Even if you lose individual tricks, capturing 6 or 7 Diamonds will guarantee you 2 points at the end of the round (Diamond count + 7 of Diamonds).",
